**Corollary 5.2 (extended isometry).** The extended interleaving and bottleneck distances are equal, including infinity, because their feasible nonnegative $\epsilon$ sets are equal. This retains $\epsilon=0$, zero and empty diagrams, critical length $2\epsilon$, unequal essential counts and unrestricted tails. It is not merely an infimum-with-slack stability statement. The fully faithful universe-lift functor preserves and reflects both natural transformations and both composite equations, so the equivalence concerns the original real extensions, not only their lifted representations.

